<title>USA: Lockheed Martin commercial paper raised.</title>
<headline>Lockheed Martin commercial paper raised.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Tuesday it raised its rating on Lockheed Martin Corp's commercial paper to D-one-minus from D-two and reaffirmed the company's senior debt rating of single-A-minus.</p>
<p>The higher commercial paper rating reflects the defense contractor's significant progress in reducing commerical paper -- or short-term debt -- during 1996 and prospects for further reduction in 1997, Duff &amp; Phelps said.</p>
<p>Lockheed Martin shares rose 1-3/8 to 85-3/4 Tuesday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
